    <bpmn:process id="W_W1565" name="W1565. Annual Insurance Portfolio Review, Coverage Gap Analysis &amp; Market Benchmarking for Policy Renewal" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Annual insurance renewal cycle (typically 60–90 days before policy expiration); or significant business change (new store format, new service offering, major acquisition); or major claim event revealing coverage gap
Frequency: Annual comprehensive review; quarterly monitoring of coverage adequacy
Volume: ~15–20 insurance policies across 5 legal entities covering: property (200 stores + 4 DCs + HQ), general liability, product liability, workers&#x27; compensation, motor vehicle (fleet), business interruption, cyber liability, professional liability, directors &amp; officers, and cargo/transit
Owner: CFO
Participants: CFO, Insurance Coordinator, COO, VP Legal &amp; Compliance, External Insurance Broker, External Actuary, CEO (final approval)
Source: workflow W1565 — Annual Insurance Portfolio Review, Coverage Gap Analysis &amp; Market Benchmarking for Policy Renewal</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1565_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1565_Lane1" name="Insurance Coordinator">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1565_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1565_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1565_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1565_Lane2" name="CFO">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1565_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1565_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1565_Lane3" name="External Insurance Broker">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1565_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1565_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1565_Start5" name="Annual insurance renewal cycle (typically 60–90 days before policy expiration); or…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1565_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1565_Task6" name="Current portfolio inventory">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Current portfolio inventory: Insurance Coordinator compiles complete insurance portfolio inventory: (a) all active policies: insurer, policy number, coverage type, insured amount, premium, deductible, policy period, key exclusions; (b) insured assets: all 200 stores (replacement cost per W1445 construction cost), 4 DCs, HQ, inventory value (WAC per model company profile Section 6.3), fleet (owned vehicles), equipment; (c) claims history: 3-year rolling claims by policy type, frequency, and severity; (d) loss ratio (claims paid ÷ premiums) by policy type — loss ratio &gt; 60% may trigger premium increase at renewal
Responsible (R): Insurance Coordinator
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 8 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1565_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1565_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1565_Task7" name="Coverage gap analysis">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Coverage gap analysis: CFO and VP Legal identify coverage gaps: (a) new stores opened during the year: are they added to property policy or require separate coverage?; (b) new business activities: ecommerce delivery per W19 (are third-party delivery partners covered?), tool rental per W139 (customer liability), installation services per W795 (workmanship/warranty liability); (c) emerging risks: cyber liability (customer data breach per RA 10173), climate change (increasing typhoon intensity), supply chain disruption (business interruption coverage for import delays); (d) intercompany coverage: are all 5 legal entities properly covered? intercompany transactions per W14 may create coverage complexities; (e) regulatory requirements: DOLE-mandated workers&#x27; compensation, LGU-required liability insurance for business permits per W54
Responsible (R): CFO / VP Legal
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: 4–6 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1565_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1565_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1565_Task8" name="Market benchmarking">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Market benchmarking: External Insurance Broker conducts market benchmarking: (a) obtain competitive quotes from 3–5 insurers per policy type; (b) compare: (i) premium rates (per PHP 1,000 of coverage), (ii) deductible options, (iii) coverage limits and sub-limits, (iv) key exclusions and endorsements, (v) insurer financial strength rating (Philippine market: assess AM Best or local rating agency ratings); (c) identify potential savings: if current insurer is &gt; 10% above market average, negotiate or switch; (d) evaluate alternative structures: (i) higher deductibles for lower premiums (self-insure smaller losses), (ii) blanket coverage vs. scheduled per-location (blanket may be more efficient for 200 locations), (iii) captive insurance feasibility (if BuildRight reaches sufficient scale)
Responsible (R): External Insurance Broker / CFO
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: 20–30 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1565_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1565_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1565_Task9" name="Renewal negotiation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Renewal negotiation: CFO negotiates renewal with incumbent insurer or transitions to new insurer: (a) present loss history and risk mitigation measures (W848 BCP, W1450 earthquake protocol, W927 fire safety) to demonstrate risk quality; (b) negotiate: (i) premium rate (target: ≤ market average), (ii) deductible per risk type (balance: lower deductible = higher premium but more predictable costs), (iii) coverage enhancements (remove or reduce key exclusions), (iv) multi-year policy (2–3 year terms lock in rates); (c) VP Legal reviews policy wording for coverage triggers, conditions, and exclusions; (d) CEO approves final policy terms and premium for policies &gt; PHP 5M annual premium
Responsible (R): CFO / VP Legal / External Broker
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: 10–15 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1565_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1565_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1565_Task10" name="Policy implementation &amp; communication">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Policy implementation &amp; communication: (a) Insurance Coordinator distributes policy documents to all stakeholders: (i) Store Managers — certificate of insurance for their location (required for LGU business permits per W54), (ii) COO — claims procedure quick reference, (iii) VP Legal — full policy documentation, (iv) CHRO — workers&#x27; compensation procedure; (b) update ERP insurance module with new policy terms, premium schedules, and claim contact information; (c) calendar next renewal date with 90-day advance preparation trigger
Responsible (R): Insurance Coordinator
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 4–6 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1565_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1565_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1565_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1565_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1565_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-321 (ensure controlled execution — Insurance Claims &amp; Policy Management (PA-26.3).) | - operational: CFO review and approval gate
Owner: CFO</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1565_Assoc13" sourceRef="W1565_Annotation12" targetRef="W1565_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1565_Flow14" sourceRef="W1565_Start5" targetRef="W1565_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1565_Flow15" sourceRef="W1565_Task6" targetRef="W1565_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1565_Flow16" sourceRef="W1565_Task7" targetRef="W1565_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1565_Flow17" sourceRef="W1565_Task8" targetRef="W1565_Task9" />
