    <bpmn:process id="W_W1566" name="W1566. Store-Level Slip-and-Fall, Customer Injury &amp; Third-Party Liability Incident Response &amp; Claims Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer injury reported at store (slip-and-fall, falling merchandise, equipment injury, parking lot incident); or third-party property damage claim; or customer allegation of injury without immediate evidence
Frequency: ~20–40 customer injury incidents/month chain-wide (~0.1–0.2 incidents/store/month); ~5–10 result in liability claims/year
Volume: Majority are minor (bruises, minor cuts requiring first aid only); ~10–15% require medical treatment beyond first aid; ~2–5% result in formal liability claims or litigation
Owner: Store Manager (immediate response); VP Legal (claim management)
Participants: Store Manager, Customer Service Rep, VP Legal, Insurance Coordinator, LP Officer, Maintenance/Utility, External Legal Counsel (for litigation), Customer
Source: workflow W1566 — Store-Level Slip-and-Fall, Customer Injury &amp; Third-Party Liability Incident Response &amp; Claims Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1566_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1566_Lane1" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1566_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1566_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1566_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1566_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1566_Lane2" name="LP Officer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1566_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1566_Lane3" name="Insurance Coordinator">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1566_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1566_Lane4" name="VP Legal">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1566_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1566_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1566_Start6" name="Customer injury reported at store (slip-and-fall, falling merchandise, equipment injury…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1566_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1566_Task7" name="Immediate incident response">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Immediate incident response (within minutes): (a) Store Manager or nearest staff member: (i) ensure customer safety — remove hazards, stop the activity causing injury; (ii) provide first aid from store first aid kit per W140 (OHS); (iii) if injury appears serious (broken bone, head injury, heavy bleeding): call emergency medical services (911 or local hospital ambulance); (iv) do not move a customer with suspected spinal injury; (v) Store Manager notifies LP Officer for immediate scene documentation; (b) for minor injuries (bruise, small cut): offer first aid and water; ask customer if they would like to sit down; (c) for all injuries: Store Manager personally attends to the customer — shows empathy and concern; do not admit fault or liability
Responsible (R): Store Manager / LP Officer
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 10–30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1566_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1566_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1566_Task8" name="Scene documentation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Scene documentation (within 1 hour): LP Officer conducts thorough scene documentation: (a) photographs: (i) hazard that caused injury (wet floor, fallen merchandise, damaged flooring), (ii) surrounding area (wide angle shots showing context), (iii) warning signage present or absent; (b) CCTV footage: extract and preserve footage covering the incident location from 15 minutes before to 15 minutes after the incident; (c) witness statements: name, contact number, and brief description of what they saw from 2–3 witnesses (staff and other customers); (d) incident report: date, time, location (specific area of store), customer name and contact, description of what happened, customer&#x27;s account of events, staff account, first aid provided, whether emergency services called; (e) Store Manager signs incident report
Responsible (R): LP Officer / Store Manager
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 30–60 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1566_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1566_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1566_Task9" name="Customer follow-up">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Customer follow-up (within 24 hours): (a) Store Manager calls the injured customer: (i) express genuine concern for their well-being, (ii) ask about their medical status, (iii) offer to reimburse reasonable medical expenses (doctor visit, x-ray, medication) — this is a goodwill gesture, not an admission of liability (VP Legal approves reimbursement threshold: up to PHP 10,000 at Store Manager level, PHP 50,000 at COO level); (b) document customer&#x27;s account of the incident and current condition; (c) if customer indicates intent to pursue legal claim: VP Legal notified immediately
Responsible (R): Store Manager / VP Legal
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 15–30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1566_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1566_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1566_Task10" name="Insurance notification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Insurance notification (within 48 hours for incidents involving medical treatment): Insurance Coordinator submits preliminary incident report to general liability insurer: (a) incident details from Step 2; (b) customer information; (c) preliminary assessment of potential liability; (d) early notification preserves BuildRight&#x27;s right to claim even if the incident does not develop into a formal claim; (e) insurer assigns claim adjuster for incidents involving medical treatment
Responsible (R): Insurance Coordinator
Accountable (A): VP Legal
Duration: 30 min/incident</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1566_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1566_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1566_Task11" name="Formal claim management">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Formal claim management (if customer files claim or lawsuit): VP Legal manages formal claim process: (a) engage External Legal Counsel for claims exceeding PHP 100,000 or involving litigation; (b) legal defense strategy: (i) review all documentation (incident report, CCTV, witness statements, maintenance logs for the hazard area), (ii) assess liability: was BuildRight negligent? (failure to maintain safe premises, inadequate warning signage, improper merchandise stacking), (iii) assess damages: medical expenses, lost income, pain and suffering (Philippine courts award lower damages than US courts, but awards can still reach PHP 500K–5M for serious injuries); (c) settlement vs. litigation decision: (i) for clear BuildRight liability with moderate damages: settle within insurance deductible to avoid litigation costs, (ii) for disputed liability or excessive demands: defend through litigation; (d) coordinate with insurer per W857 for claim payment
Responsible (R): VP Legal / External Counsel / Insurance Coordinator
Accountable (A): CEO (for claims &gt; PHP 1M)
Duration: Variable (weeks to months)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1566_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1566_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1566_Task12" name="Corrective action &amp; prevention">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Corrective action &amp; prevention: After every customer injury incident: (a) Store Manager implements immediate corrective action: (i) wet floor: deploy additional mats and warning signs, fix leak source, (ii) falling merchandise: restack properly, review shelf load limits per W47 (store facility maintenance), install shelf safety clips, (iii) parking lot: repair pothole, improve lighting, re-mark pedestrian zones per W1537; (b) COO reviews corrective action adequacy; (c) LP Officer includes incident in monthly loss prevention report per W538 for chain-wide pattern analysis: (i) incident frequency by type and store, (ii) identify stores with above-average incident rates for targeted safety inspections
Responsible (R): Store Manager / LP Officer / COO
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 1–2 hours/incident</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1566_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1566_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1566_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1566_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1566_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-321 (ensure controlled execution — Insurance Claims &amp; Policy Management (PA-26.3).) | - operational: incident form enforces mandatory fields and photo prompts before submission; LP Officer verifies scene-documentation completeness
Owner: Store Manager (immediate response); VP Legal (claim management)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1566_Assoc15" sourceRef="W1566_Annotation14" targetRef="W1566_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1566_Flow16" sourceRef="W1566_Start6" targetRef="W1566_Task7" />
